+// PSH bit 2 (b2364, plan_push_1113.md 'PSH bit 2 FINAL FORM', Deep's zone re-cut; owner 13 Nov: "if we play aggressive with Issac, he has
+// dash and can invest in health so lives, and Cassi can slowly play more passive and rely on her group more" + "Cassi can play more
+// aggressive at the start, but as she gets outstated she should play more passive"). Not zone-gated. 0 = v860. Always (bit 2): Issac,
+// while Cassi is within a visible foe's two-turn reach, keeps his dash as the escape (no dash landing nearer the nearest foe). While
+// Q = the strongest visible foe within 8's maxHp x (Str + Focus) / Cassi's >= PSH_CG_X10 / 10 (on; off again below PSH_CG_X10 / 10 - 1;
+// PSH_CG_X10 0 = always): Cassi takes no step or dash that brings her nearer a visible foe where she would be the body nearest it
+// (nearer than Issac and than her nearest other mate), nor one nearer the nearest foe that leaves her more than PSH_MATE_R from her
+// nearest non-Issac mate within 8. The pair's strength already uses the weaker body's health (CI2 decision 6, link_friend_h).
+// RC C1038: consulted only while fight_stage runs (the SPZ scope), never for a game-ending deny cast, a capture or an escape; Issac's
+// trigger is a foe's next-turn reach + 1.
+// Arms: A "PSH_BITS=2" (PSH_CG_X10 50), B "PSH_BITS=2 PSH_CG_X10=0".
+#define PSH_BITS 0
+#define PSH_CG_X10 50
+#define PSH_MATE_R 4
+inline const volatile int PSH_TAB[3] = { 0x50534832, PSH_BITS, PSH_CG_X10 };
+#define PSH_ON(b) ((PSH_TAB[1] & (b)) != 0)
